-Settings → Identity (`/settings/p6rIdentity`) shows the provider-verified identity
+Settings → Identity (`/settings/p6rIdentity`) shows the resolved identity
 for your current connection. `bb settings p6r-identity --json` and
 `sdk.system.p6rIdentity()` expose the same check for their own request; a local CLI
 connection need not resolve to the same person as a browser behind a trusted
-proxy. An unconfigured instance retains native local behavior. An unavailable
-configured provider does not fall back to a claimed name.
+proxy. An unconfigured instance retains native local behavior. Requests through
+the owned Tailnet listener use a stable machine actor when verified person
+evidence is unavailable. Local CLI requests use the separate loopback listener.
 
 For Tailscale Serve deployments, `BB_TAILNET_IDENTITY_OWNED_HOST` automatically
 selects the installed Identity Boundaries provider and standard loopback ingress.
 No separate `BB_P6R_IDENTITY_BOUNDARY` opt-in is needed; an explicit custom boundary
-still takes precedence. Requests without verified person evidence use machine
-attribution. Validate your own identity through your browser connection.
+still takes precedence. Set `BB_TAILNET_INGRESS_PORT` to the distinct loopback
+port served by Tailscale Serve. Validate your own identity through your browser
+connection; the local CLI connection can retain machine attribution.
 
 New browser sends retain their verified author separately from message text,
 including queued sends and retries. Older unattributed messages remain unknown.
